# Frontend

## UI system

Tokens in `src/styles/tokens.css` are the source of truth for color, type, and spacing. The design-reference kit informs visuals; don’t paste kit code wholesale into the app.

Collaboration layouts use the full viewport on wide screens; constrain width only where readability demands it (e.g. auth). **PWA usability, touch, and reflow:** `mobile-pwa-ux.mdc`.

## Layout discipline

Scrollable regions need a bounded flex chain (`min-h-0`, `flex-1`, intentional `overflow`). Fixed chrome (header, bottom bar) accounts for safe-area insets via shared offset tokens.

Overlays and tooltips escape clipping ancestors—use portals or fixed positioning when content must not be truncated by `overflow-hidden` shells.

## Navigation and context

The user’s current project, topic, and session travel with API and realtime calls—scope is never “whatever the server assumes.” One canvas component serves global and project graphs; positions persist through the topology API.

## Types and API

Strict TypeScript; shared response shapes live in `src/lib/types`. REST and WebSocket/SSE share the same base URL strategy.

## Chat surfaces

Multiple chat experiences exist (private assistant vs shared thread); treat them as different transport and persistence models. Extend documented surfaces; don’t revive deprecated routes as shortcuts.

Feature parity across surfaces matters: if context attachment exists in one composer, design for the others or document intentional omission.

## Ship check

`npm run build` must pass before you call frontend work done.
